import{_ as a,o as t,c as s,a2 as i}from"./chunks/framework.DncwoWA8.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Set up optional authoring skills","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"maintenance/authoring-skills.md","filePath":"maintenance/authoring-skills.md"}'),n={name:"maintenance/authoring-skills.md"};function o(r,e,l,c,d,p){return t(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<h1 id="set-up-optional-authoring-skills" tabindex="-1">Set up optional authoring skills <a class="header-anchor" href="#set-up-optional-authoring-skills" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Set up optional authoring skills&quot;">​</a></h1><p>This setup is for contributors working in this repository. It is separate from the cross-project Node.js <code>sync-skills</code> CLI and from instruction-document maintenance.</p><h2 id="review-the-installer" tabindex="-1">Review the installer <a class="header-anchor" href="#review-the-installer" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Review the installer&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Read <a href="https://github.com/dragoscirjan/ai/blob/main/scripts/install-dev-skills.sh" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><code>scripts/install-dev-skills.sh</code></a> and the <a href="../../catalog/skill-catalog.yaml">catalog</a> before approving downloads. The Bash script groups external authoring skills by source and installs them from upstream <code>main</code> branches. Those inputs are mutable. Review and trust the sources before running them.</p><p>You need Bash 4 or newer, Node.js 24, npm/npx, and Git. From the repository root, after approving this setup:</p><div class="language-sh vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes catppuccin-latte catppuccin-mocha vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#1E66F5;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#89B4FA;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;">bash</span><span style="--shiki-light:#40A02B;--shiki-dark:#A6E3A1;"> scripts/install-dev-skills.sh</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The script installs dependencies under the ignored <code>.agents/skills/external/&lt;name&gt;/</code> directory. It can move existing flat installations there; existing categorized adaptations and external-folder copies remain unchanged. It does not install globally or synchronize project instruction files. Reload the agent&#39;s skill discovery afterward, for example <code>/reload</code> in Pi.</p><p>Catalogued upstream instructions are installation requirements only when selected by the project or a skill&#39;s declared <code>requires</code> array. A catalog entry alone does not authorize a fetch. Missing required skills stop the affected workflow until the user arranges approved setup.</p><h2 id="preserve-source-ownership" tabindex="-1">Preserve source ownership <a class="header-anchor" href="#preserve-source-ownership" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Preserve source ownership&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Use catalogued upstream sources for unchanged external skills. Do not silently edit ignored upstream copies and describe them as maintained source. Substantial adaptations need their own reviewed source and catalog provenance. Preserve supporting files and legal notices, and exclude unwanted provider metadata from managed outputs.</p><p>The maintained <code>code-review</code>, <code>grill-me</code>, and <code>tdd</code> variants now live in the categorized source directories. The authoring installer keeps those sources rather than downloading replacements when no older ignored copy is present. If an older copy under <code>.agents/skills/external/</code> duplicates a maintained skill, inspect and preserve it outside discovery or approve its exact removal before reloading. Do not discard local changes or keep two discovered copies of the same name.</p><p>The Node.js CLI copies reviewed variants directly; it does not adapt instructions or call an LLM during synchronization. New upstream versions need normal source review before a maintained update is published. The guard against future unprepared remote adaptations stays in place.</p><h2 id="check-skill-independence" tabindex="-1">Check skill independence <a class="header-anchor" href="#check-skill-independence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Check skill independence&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Review each complete portable package, not only its SKILL.md. Operational cross-skill names, links, helper imports, and invocation examples must refer only to self or declared requirements. Keep skill overview READMEs focused on intent, real dependencies, and verified factual origin or inspiration. Short usage examples and optional standalone install instructions are allowed. Install instructions use the pinned acquisition tool without the sync CLI and preserve the complete skill folder, including required supporting and legal files. An attribution is not a handoff or dependency. Keep operating instructions in SKILL.md and supporting documents, legal files separate, and collection setup in repository documentation. Nested technical READMEs are not skill overviews. Do not add dependencies merely to keep a recommendation. Source checks and acquired-package verification enforce this boundary.</p><h2 id="check-and-recover" tabindex="-1">Check and recover <a class="header-anchor" href="#check-and-recover" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Check and recover&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Run the network-free installer tests from the repository root:</p><div class="language-sh vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes catppuccin-latte catppuccin-mocha vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#1E66F5;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#89B4FA;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;">node</span><span style="--shiki-light:#40A02B;--shiki-dark:#A6E3A1;"> --test</span><span style="--shiki-light:#40A02B;--shiki-dark:#A6E3A1;"> scripts/install-dev-skills.test.mjs</span></span></code></pre></div><p>If a source or command fails, inspect the reported installation and missing skill. Do not substitute another skill, initialize tools, change trust, or rerun installations without the necessary approval. The retired <code>sync-my-skills</code> manager, its parser setup, and its personal commands are not required by this authoring installer.</p>',18)])])}const m=a(n,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
